DO  - 10.5555/lls-example.0002
AB  - Objective: To compare supervised aquatic exercise with a waiting list in adults with chronic non-specific low back pain. Design: Randomised controlled trial with blinded outcome assessment. Participants: 96 adults aged 18 to 70 years with back pain for at least three months. Intervention: Twice-weekly supervised aquatic exercise sessions for 10 weeks. Outcomes: Pain intensity on a numerical rating scale and disability on the Roland-Morris questionnaire. Results: Aquatic exercise reduced pain and disability more than the waiting list at 10 weeks.
