AB  - Background: Graded activity and strengthening exercise are both used for chronic low back pain. Methods: Adults with non-specific back pain for more than 12 weeks were randomized to graded activity or physiotherapist-supervised strengthening exercise for 12 weeks. Outcomes were pain intensity, disability and global perceived effect at 3, 6 and 12 months. Results: Both groups improved; strengthening exercise led to slightly larger reductions in disability at 3 months, with no difference at 12 months.
